{"format":1,"manifest":{"name":"laravel-models","publisher":"vyloxi","version":"1.0.0","displayName":"Laravel Models","description":"Write the @property docblock of an Eloquent model from your migrations, generate $fillable and casts, list relations and add a relation method.","engines":{"ferrum":"^0.1.0"},"categories":["Tools"],"icon":"icon.png","repository":"https://github.com/voukengdongmofrankysteve/ferrum-market","license":"MIT","main":"extension.js","activationEvents":["onCommand:laravelModels.docblock","onCommand:laravelModels.fillable","onCommand:laravelModels.casts","onCommand:laravelModels.columns","onCommand:laravelModels.relations","onCommand:laravelModels.addRelation"],"permissions":["workspace.read"],"contributes":{"commands":[{"command":"laravelModels.docblock","title":"Write @property Docblock from Migrations","category":"Laravel Models"},{"command":"laravelModels.fillable","title":"Insert $fillable from Migrations","category":"Laravel Models"},{"command":"laravelModels.casts","title":"Insert casts() from Migrations","category":"Laravel Models"},{"command":"laravelModels.columns","title":"Pick a Column of This Model...","category":"Laravel Models"},{"command":"laravelModels.relations","title":"Jump to a Relation in This Model...","category":"Laravel Models"},{"command":"laravelModels.addRelation","title":"Add a Relation Method...","category":"Laravel Models"}],"configuration":{"title":"Laravel Models","properties":{"laravelModels.queryMethod":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"Also write a @method static query() line in the docblock."}}}}},"files":{"icon.png":{"encoding":"base64","content":""},"extension.js":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"// Laravel Models: write the @property docblock of an Eloquent model from your migrations, fill $fillable and casts, and list a model's relations.\r\n// It reads database/migrations/*.php as text (Schema::create and Schema::table), so it works without a database connection.\r\n\r\nconst IRREGULAR = { person: 'people', man: 'men', woman: 'women', child: 'children', foot: 'feet', tooth: 'teeth', mouse: 'mice', goose: 'geese', criterion: 'criteria', datum: 'data', medium: 'media', analysis: 'analyses', index: 'indices', matrix: 'matrices', status: 'statuses', bus: 'buses' };\r\nconst UNCOUNTABLE = new Set(['equipment', 'information', 'rice', 'money', 'species', 'series', 'fish', 'sheep', 'news', 'media', 'data']);\r\n\r\nfunction pluralize(word) {\r\n  const w = word.toLowerCase();\r\n  if (UNCOUNTABLE.has(w)) return w;\r\n  if (IRREGULAR[w]) return IRREGULAR[w];\r\n  if (/[^aeiou]y$/.test(w)) return w.slice(0, -1) + 'ies';\r\n  if (/(s|x|z|ch|sh)$/.test(w)) return w + 'es';\r\n  if (/[^aeiou]o$/.test(w) && ['hero', 'potato', 'tomato', 'echo', 'veto'].includes(w)) return w + 'es';\r\n  if (/fe?$/.test(w) && ['knife', 'wife', 'life', 'leaf', 'half', 'wolf', 'shelf'].includes(w)) return w.replace(/fe?$/, 'ves');\r\n  return w + 's';\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst snake = (s) => s.replace(/([a-z0-9])([A-Z])/g, '$1_$2').replace(/([A-Z]+)([A-Z][a-z])/g, '$1_$2').toLowerCase();\r\n\r\n/** The table of a model class: the default is the plural of the snake case class name, like Eloquent. */\r\nfunction tableFor(className) {\r\n  const parts = snake(className).split('_');\r\n  parts[parts.length - 1] = pluralize(parts[parts.length - 1]);\r\n  return parts.join('_');\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst CARBON = '\\\\Illuminate\\\\Support\\\\Carbon';\r\nconst TYPE = {\r\n  id: 'int', bigIncrements: 'int', increments: 'int', mediumIncrements: 'int', smallIncrements: 'int', tinyIncrements: 'int',\r\n  integer: 'int', bigInteger: 'int', mediumInteger: 'int', smallInteger: 'int', tinyInteger: 'int', unsignedBigInteger: 'int', unsignedInteger: 'int', unsignedMediumInteger: 'int', unsignedSmallInteger: 'int', unsignedTinyInteger: 'int', foreignId: 'int', year: 'int',\r\n  string: 'string', char: 'string', text: 'string', mediumText: 'string', longText: 'string', tinyText: 'string', uuid: 'string', ulid: 'string', ipAddress: 'string', macAddress: 'string', enum: 'string', binary: 'string', rememberToken: 'string', foreignUuid: 'string', foreignUlid: 'string', time: 'string', timeTz: 'string',\r\n  boolean: 'bool', decimal: 'float', double: 'float', float: 'float', unsignedDecimal: 'float',\r\n  json: 'array', jsonb: 'array', set: 'array',\r\n  date: CARBON, dateTime: CARBON, dateTimeTz: CARBON, timestamp: CARBON, timestampTz: CARBON,\r\n};\r\n\r\n/** Reads the columns a migration file adds, drops or renames, in the order they appear. */\r\nfunction parseMigration(text) {\r\n  const ops = [];\r\n  const blocks = [...text.matchAll(/Schema::(create|table)\\(\\s*['\"]([\\w.]+)['\"]\\s*,\\s*(?:function|fn)\\s*\\(\\s*(?:Blueprint\\s+)?\\$\\w+\\s*\\)\\s*(?:use\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\\s*)?(?:\\{|=>)/g)];\r\n  for (const b of blocks) {\r\n    const table = b[2];\r\n    const start = b.index + b[0].length;\r\n    let depth = 1;\r\n    let i = start;\r\n    for (; i < text.length && depth > 0; i++) {\r\n      if (text[i] === '{') depth++;\r\n      else if (text[i] === '}') depth--;\r\n    }\r\n    const body = text.slice(start, i);\r\n    const kind = b[1];\r\n    for (const line of body.split(/;\\s*\\n|;\\s*$/)) {\r\n      const m = /\\$\\w+->(\\w+)\\(([^)]*)\\)((?:->\\w+\\([^)]*\\))*)/.exec(line.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim());\r\n      if (!m) continue;\r\n      const [, method, argText, mods] = m;\r\n      const args = [...argText.matchAll(/'([^']*)'|\"([^\"]*)\"|(\\[[^\\]]*\\])|([^,\\s]+)/g)].map((a) => a[1] ?? a[2] ?? a[3] ?? a[4]);\r\n      const nullable = /->nullable\\(/.test(mods);\r\n      if (method === 'dropColumn') {\r\n        const names = argText.includes('[') ? [...argText.matchAll(/'([^']+)'/g)].map((x) => x[1]) : args;\r\n        for (const n of names) ops.push({ table, op: 'drop', name: n });\r\n      } else if (method === 'renameColumn') ops.push({ table, op: 'rename', from: args[0], name: args[1] });\r\n      else if (method === 'dropTimestamps') {\r\n        ops.push({ table, op: 'drop', name: 'created_at' }, { table, op: 'drop', name: 'updated_at' });\r\n      } else if (method === 'dropSoftDeletes') ops.push({ table, op: 'drop', name: 'deleted_at' });\r\n      else if (method === 'dropRememberToken') ops.push({ table, op: 'drop', name: 'remember_token' });\r\n      else if (method === 'timestamps' || method === 'nullableTimestamps') ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: 'created_at', type: CARBON, nullable: true }, { table, op: 'add', name: 'updated_at', type: CARBON, nullable: true });\r\n      else if (method === 'softDeletes' || method === 'softDeletesTz') ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: args[0] || 'deleted_at', type: CARBON, nullable: true });\r\n      else if (method === 'rememberToken') ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: 'remember_token', type: 'string', nullable: true });\r\n      else if (method === 'morphs' || method === 'nullableMorphs' || method === 'uuidMorphs' || method === 'ulidMorphs') {\r\n        ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: args[0] + '_type', type: 'string', nullable: method.startsWith('nullable') }, { table, op: 'add', name: args[0] + '_id', type: method.startsWith('uuid') || method.startsWith('ulid') ? 'string' : 'int', nullable: method.startsWith('nullable') });\r\n      } else if (method === 'id') ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: args[0] || 'id', type: 'int', nullable: false });\r\n      else if (TYPE[method] && args[0] && /^[A-Za-z_]\\w*$/.test(args[0])) ops.push({ table, op: 'add', name: args[0], type: TYPE[method], nullable: nullable || (kind === 'table' && false), mod: method });\r\n      void kind;\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return ops;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** The columns of every table after all the migrations, given in file order. */\r\nfunction buildSchema(migrations) {\r\n  const tables = {};\r\n  for (const text of migrations) {\r\n    for (const op of parseMigration(text)) {\r\n      const t = (tables[op.table] ||= []);\r\n      if (op.op === 'add') {\r\n        const i = t.findIndex((c) => c.name === op.name);\r\n        if (i >= 0) t[i] = op;\r\n        else t.push(op);\r\n      } else if (op.op === 'drop') tables[op.table] = t.filter((c) => c.name !== op.name);\r\n      else if (op.op === 'rename') {\r\n        const c = t.find((x) => x.name === op.from);\r\n        if (c) c.name = op.name;\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n  return tables;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction docblock(columns, className, opts = {}) {\r\n  const rows = columns.map((c) => ' * @property ' + (c.nullable ? c.type + '|null' : c.type) + ' $' + c.name);\r\n  void className;\r\n  const head = ['/**', ...rows];\r\n  if (opts.query) head.push(' *', ' * @method static \\\\Illuminate\\\\Database\\\\Eloquent\\\\Builder|' + className + ' query()');\r\n  head.push(' */');\r\n  return head.join('\\n');\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst NOT_FILLABLE = new Set(['id', 'created_at', 'updated_at', 'deleted_at', 'remember_token']);\r\nfunction fillable(columns) {\r\n  return columns.map((c) => c.name).filter((n) => !NOT_FILLABLE.has(n));\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Suggested $casts for columns whose type is not plain text or a number. */\r\nfunction casts(columns) {\r\n  const out = {};\r\n  for (const c of columns) {\r\n    if (c.type === 'bool') out[c.name] = 'boolean';\r\n    else if (c.type === 'array') out[c.name] = 'array';\r\n    else if (c.type === CARBON && !['created_at', 'updated_at', 'deleted_at'].includes(c.name)) out[c.name] = c.mod === 'date' ? 'date' : 'datetime';\r\n    else if (c.type === 'float' && c.mod === 'decimal') out[c.name] = 'decimal:2';\r\n    else if (c.name === 'password') out[c.name] = 'hashed';\r\n    else if (c.name === 'email_verified_at') out[c.name] = 'datetime';\r\n  }\r\n  return out;\r\n}\r\n\r\nconst REL = ['hasOne', 'hasMany', 'belongsTo', 'belongsToMany', 'hasOneThrough', 'hasManyThrough', 'morphOne', 'morphMany', 'morphTo', 'morphToMany', 'morphedByMany'];\r\nfunction relations(source) {\r\n  const out = [];\r\n  const re = new RegExp('function\\\\s+(\\\\w+)\\\\s*\\\\([^)]*\\\\)\\\\s*(?::\\\\s*[\\\\w\\\\\\\\|?]+\\\\s*)?\\\\{\\\\s*return\\\\s+\\\\$this->(' + REL.join('|') + ')\\\\(\\\\s*([\\\\\\\\\\\\w]+)?(?:::class)?', 'g');\r\n  let m;\r\n  while ((m = re.exec(source))) out.push({ name: m[1], type: m[2], related: m[3] ? m[3].split('\\\\').pop() : null, line: source.slice(0, m.index).split('\\n').length });\r\n  return out;\r\n}\r\n\r\nfunction classInfo(source) {\r\n  const m = /class\\s+(\\w+)\\s+extends\\s+([\\\\\\w]+)/.exec(source);\r\n  const table = /\\$table\\s*=\\s*['\"]([\\w.]+)['\"]/.exec(source);\r\n  return m ? { name: m[1], extends: m[2], table: table ? table[1] : null, line: source.slice(0, m.index).split('\\n').length - 1 } : null;\r\n}\r\n\r\n/** Puts the docblock right above \"class\", replacing a docblock this extension wrote earlier. */\r\nfunction applyDocblock(source, block) {\r\n  const marker = '@property';\r\n  const re = /\\/\\*\\*(?:(?!\\*\\/)[\\s\\S])*?\\*\\/\\s*\\n(?=(?:final\\s+|abstract\\s+)?class\\s)/;\r\n  const m = re.exec(source);\r\n  if (m && m[0].includes(marker)) return source.replace(re, block + '\\n');\r\n  return source.replace(/^((?:final\\s+|abstract\\s+)?class\\s)/m, block + '\\n$1');\r\n}\r\n\r\nexports._test = { pluralize, tableFor, parseMigration, buildSchema, docblock, fillable, casts, relations, classInfo, applyDocblock, snake };\r\n\r\nexports.activate = function (context) {\r\n  const root = () => ferrum.workspace.root;\r\n  const full = (p) => (/^([a-zA-Z]:|[\\\\/])/.test(p) ? p : root() + (root().includes('\\\\') ? '\\\\' : '/') + p);\r\n\r\n  async function schema() {\r\n    const files = (await ferrum.workspace.listFiles('database/migrations/*.php')).filter((f) => /database[\\\\/]migrations[\\\\/][^\\\\/]+\\.php$/.test(f)).sort();\r\n    const texts = [];\r\n    for (const f of files) {\r\n      try {\r\n        texts.push(await ferrum.workspace.readFile(full(f)));\r\n      } catch {\r\n        /* an unreadable migration is skipped */\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n    return { tables: buildSchema(texts), count: files.length };\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  async function modelContext() {\r\n    const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n    if (!doc) {\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a model file first.', 'warn');\r\n      return null;\r\n    }\r\n    const info = classInfo(doc.text);\r\n    if (!info) {\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('No class found in this file.', 'warn');\r\n      return null;\r\n    }\r\n    if (!root()) {\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Open the Laravel project folder first.', 'warn');\r\n      return null;\r\n    }\r\n    const s = await schema();\r\n    const table = info.table || tableFor(info.name);\r\n    const columns = s.tables[table];\r\n    if (!columns || !columns.length) {\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('No migration creates the table \"' + table + '\"' + (s.count ? ' (looked at ' + s.count + ' migrations).' : '. There are no migrations in database/migrations.') + ' Set protected $table if the name is different.', 'warn');\r\n      return null;\r\n    }\r\n    return { doc, info, table, columns };\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  context.subscriptions.push(\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.docblock', async () => {\r\n      const c = await modelContext();\r\n      if (!c) return;\r\n      const block = docblock(c.columns, c.info.name, { query: ferrum.settings.get('laravelModels.queryMethod') === true });\r\n      const out = applyDocblock(c.doc.text, block);\r\n      if (out === c.doc.text) return ferrum.window.showMessage('The docblock is already up to date.');\r\n      await ferrum.editor.replace({ start: { line: 0, col: 0 }, end: { line: c.doc.lineCount, col: 0 } }, out);\r\n      ferrum.window.showMessage('Wrote ' + c.columns.length + ' @property lines for table \"' + c.table + '\".');\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.fillable', async () => {\r\n      const c = await modelContext();\r\n      if (!c) return;\r\n      const list = fillable(c.columns);\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert('protected $fillable = [\\n' + list.map((n) => \"    '\" + n + \"',\").join('\\n') + '\\n];');\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.casts', async () => {\r\n      const c = await modelContext();\r\n      if (!c) return;\r\n      const k = casts(c.columns);\r\n      const keys = Object.keys(k);\r\n      if (!keys.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No column needs a cast.');\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert('protected function casts(): array\\n{\\n    return [\\n' + keys.map((n) => \"        '\" + n + \"' => '\" + k[n] + \"',\").join('\\n') + '\\n    ];\\n}');\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.columns', async () => {\r\n      const c = await modelContext();\r\n      if (!c) return;\r\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(c.columns.map((col) => ({ label: col.name, detail: col.type + (col.nullable ? ' (nullable)' : '') })), { placeholder: 'Columns of ' + c.table + ' (pick one to insert its name)' });\r\n      if (p) await ferrum.editor.insert(p.label);\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.relations', async () => {\r\n      const doc = await ferrum.editor.active();\r\n      if (!doc) return ferrum.window.showMessage('Open a model file first.', 'warn');\r\n      const list = relations(doc.text);\r\n      if (!list.length) return ferrum.window.showMessage('No relations found in this file.');\r\n      const p = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(list.map((r) => ({ label: r.name, detail: r.type + (r.related ? ' ' + r.related : ''), line: r.line })), { placeholder: 'Relations in this model' });\r\n      if (p) await ferrum.editor.setSelection({ line: p.line - 1, col: 0 });\r\n    }),\r\n    ferrum.commands.register('laravelModels.addRelation', async () => {\r\n      const type = await ferrum.window.showQuickPick(['hasMany', 'hasOne', 'belongsTo', 'belongsToMany', 'morphMany', 'morphTo'].map((t) => ({ label: t })), { placeholder: 'Relation type' });\r\n      if (!type) return;\r\n      const model = type.label === 'morphTo' ? '' : await ferrum.window.showInputBox({ prompt: 'Related model', placeholder: 'Post' });\r\n      if (type.label !== 'morphTo' && !model) return;\r\n      if (model && !/^[A-Z]\\w*$/.test(model)) return ferrum.window.showMessage('A model name starts with a capital letter and has only letters and digits.', 'error');\r\n      const plural = ['hasMany', 'belongsToMany', 'morphMany'].includes(type.label);\r\n      const name = type.label === 'morphTo' ? 'commentable' : (plural ? pluralize(snake(model)).replace(/_(\\w)/g, (m, c) => c.toUpperCase()) : snake(model).replace(/_(\\w)/g, (m, c) => c.toUpperCase()));\r\n      const ret = { hasMany: 'HasMany', hasOne: 'HasOne', belongsTo: 'BelongsTo', belongsToMany: 'BelongsToMany', morphMany: 'MorphMany', morphTo: 'MorphTo' }[type.label];\r\n      const arg = type.label === 'morphTo' ? '' : model + '::class' + (type.label === 'morphMany' ? \", 'commentable'\" : '');\r\n      await ferrum.editor.insert('public function ' + name + '(): ' + ret + '\\n{\\n    return $this->' + type.label + '(' + arg + ');\\n}');\r\n    }),\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n\r\nexports.deactivate = function () {};\r\n"},"README.md":{"encoding":"utf8","content":"# Laravel Models\n\nIt reads `database/migrations/*.php` as text (no database connection needed) and follows `Schema::create` and `Schema::table`: columns added, dropped and renamed, in file order.\n\n- **Write @property Docblock from Migrations** puts (or refreshes) the docblock above `class`: `@property int $id`, `@property string|null $bio`, `@property \\Illuminate\\Support\\Carbon $created_at`. Your editor and static analysers then know the attributes. Types come from the column methods (`string`, `integer`, `boolean`, `decimal`, `json`, `dateTime`, `foreignId`, `uuid`, `enum`, `timestamps`, `softDeletes`, `morphs`...).\n- **Insert $fillable from Migrations** and **Insert casts() from Migrations** write the arrays at the cursor (booleans, JSON, dates, decimals and `password` get a cast).\n- **Jump to a Relation in This Model...** lists `hasMany`, `belongsTo`, `morphTo` and the other relations in the file.\n- **Add a Relation Method...** writes a typed relation method with the usual name.\n\nThe table is `protected $table` when set, otherwise the plural of the snake case class name (`BlogPost` is `blog_posts`, `Person` is `people`).\n\nPermission: workspace.read.\n"}}}